{"photo-caribou-bull":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/caribou-bull.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Denali National Park and Preserve, Public domain, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Profile_of_a_Bull_Caribou_(7956336958).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Caribou bull: big rack with a shovel over the face, white neck mane. Cows carry antlers too, so antlers alone never mean bull."},"photo-wood-bison":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/wood-bison.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Ansgar Walk, CC BY-SA 2.5, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wood-Buffalo-NP_Waldbison_2_98-07-02.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Bison: massive forequarters, a hump, a bearded head and short black horns. Wood bison: taller hump and darker than plains bison."},"photo-cougar":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/cougar.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: National Park Service, Public domain, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mountain_Lion_in_Grand_Teton_National_Park.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Cougar: light brown cat, compact head, long heavy tail with a black tip. Any cougar with spots is a kitten: protected, and so is any cougar with it."},"photo-grey-wolf":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/grey-wolf.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Yellowstone National Park from Yellowstone NP, USA, Public domain, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Black_and_grey_wolf_(female_from_Druid_pack,%22Half_Black%22)_walking_in_road_near_Lamar_River_bridge_(16055830467).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Grey wolf: 30 to 50 kg, long legs, big feet, broad muzzle, tail carried out behind when running. Rule out a dog before you shoot."},"photo-coyote":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/coyote.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Yathin S Krishnappa, CC BY-SA 3.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Canis_latrans_(Yosemite,_2009).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Coyote: 9 to 23 kg (a wolf is 30 to 50 kg). Slim pointed muzzle, tall ears, small feet, bushy black tipped tail carried low."},"photo-canada-lynx":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/canada-lynx.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: kdee64 (Keith Williams), CC BY 2.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Canadian_lynx_by_Keith_Williams.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Canada lynx: long ear tufts, huge furry paws, long legs, grey coat with few markings, short tail with a fully black tip."},"photo-bobcat":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/bobcat.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Joyce Cory on Flickr as docentjoyce, CC BY 2.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bobcat_photo.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Bobcat: spotted tan coat, black bars on the front legs, short ear tufts, tail black on top only with a white underside. A lynx has huge furry paws and a fully black tail tip."},"photo-wolverine":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/wolverine.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: USFWS Mountain-Prairie, Public domain, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wolverine_(5249640494).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Wolverine: heavy, low slung, dark brown body, pale band along the side, bushy tail. No Region 3 season; seasons only in Regions 6, 7A and 7B, bag limit 1, Compulsory Report."},"photo-snowshoe-hare-winter":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/snowshoe-hare-winter.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: D. Gordon E. Robertson, CC BY-SA 3.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Snowshoe_Hare,_Shirleys_Bay.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Snowshoe hare: huge furred hind feet; grey brown in summer, white in winter; black ear tips."}}